From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:43:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 65/68] The rotation test runs the real bind and checks the
 Activity's own display: sync CameraXFrameSource (F19, task 29)

Two F19 test gaps, each shown by a mutation that left all 6 tests green:
- R2: window() reading the default display (the pre-F19 behaviour) instead of Activity.getDisplay(). New test:
  an Activity whose own display reports 0 while the default display is at 90 gives window 0, display 90. It fails
  under that mutation.
- R3: the tests bound through bindForTest(), a copy of the bind's steps, so the real bind without
  followRotation() (the app never following a rotation) went unnoticed. The tests now run the real bind
  (bindUseCases, package-private since Mosip26 c0e8f6a) with a mock ProcessCameraProvider; 4 of them fail under
  that mutation. "A bind that finishes after stop" now runs the bind's own clean-up (unbindAll twice, no watch).

- CameraXFrameSource from Mosip26 c0e8f6a (Part 1); engine-sync.txt: the engine commit and the source's SHA-256.
  The four jars are unchanged (synced with -SkipBuild, the branch's jars kept).
- :liveness:testDebugUnitTest: 123 passing (122 + 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
